dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.flow.diff
version 1
schema stdio.semio.flow
start body
framing record

# P2 pilot (flow): REAL binary diff frame, replacing the old `print_diff().into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut (`🔺️diff/🦀️.rs`'s old `DiffCodec::encode_diff`). `format u8` +
# `presence u8` (bit0 = `nodes` present, bit1 = `edges` present) are two REAL fixed fields; past
# that, 0-2 varint-length-prefixed opaque blobs follow (one per present collection) — modeled as one
# opaque trailing `payload` chain rather than per-segment `Cond`-guarded fields because a SECOND
# `if`-guard on a field that was itself only conditionally decoded hard-errors `eval_cond`
# (`protocol-cond-cannot-chain`, hit here for real — see this wave's report). The real Rust
# `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` stays genuinely, fully structured (`write_str_lp`/`read_str_lp`,
# `store::pack_rt`'s real varint codec) — round-trip tested independently.
header fixed 2
field format u8
field presence u8

chain payload bytes
